The flag was saved and used for the grocery list, but nowhere a cook
reads the recipe said so. The integration API gains an "optional"
field (additive) and "(optional)" on the pre-rendered line.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NQLiThQhdxj2iQfcYnJXAQ
---
 INTEGRATION.md                                               | 5 +++--
 .../com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationDtos.java   | 2 +-
 .../gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationService.java    | 5 +++--
 web/src/components/RecipeIndexCard.tsx                       | 1 +
 web/src/pages/PublicRecipePage.tsx                           | 1 +
 web/src/pages/RecipeDetailPage.tsx                           | 1 +
 6 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/INTEGRATION.md b/INTEGRATION.md
index dc586ba..8eda237 100644
--- a/INTEGRATION.md
+++ b/INTEGRATION.md
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ files it; without it both come back empty.
   "videoUrl": "https://www.tiktok.com/…",
   "ingredients": [
     { "name": "sweetened condensed milk", "quantity": "⅓", "unit": "cup",
-      "notes": null, "text": "⅓ cup sweetened condensed milk" }
+      "notes": null, "optional": false, "text": "⅓ cup sweetened condensed milk" }
   ],
   "steps": [
     "Preheat the oven to 350°F and line a small baking dish with parchment paper.",
@@ -201,7 +201,8 @@ Two things done for you, so you don't reimplement them and drift out of step wit
 
 - **`ingredients[].text`** is the whole line pre-rendered — `"⅓ cup sweetened condensed milk"`.
   `quantity` is already a fraction glyph, not `0.333`. The separate fields are there if you want
-  to lay out columns instead.
+  to lay out columns instead. An ingredient a cook can skip has `"optional": true`, and its `text`
+  ends in `(optional)`.
 - **`steps`** is the instructions split one per line with any numbering the writer typed
   (`1.`, `-`, `•`) already stripped. Render them in an `<ol>`.
 
diff --git a/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationDtos.java b/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationDtos.java
index 549d9a3..bb889a5 100644
--- a/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationDtos.java
+++ b/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationDtos.java
@@ -84,7 +84,7 @@ public class IntegrationDtos {
      * `text` is the whole line pre-rendered — "1½ cup flour, sifted" — because a dashboard
      * almost always wants to print it rather than lay out three columns.
      */
-    public record IngredientLine(String name, String quantity, String unit, String notes, String text) {
+    public record IngredientLine(String name, String quantity, String unit, String notes, boolean optional, String text) {
     }
 
     public record GroceryItem(UUID id, String name, String quantity, String unit, boolean checked) {
diff --git a/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationService.java b/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationService.java
index 7890034..90d67e3 100644
--- a/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationService.java
+++ b/backend/src/main/java/com/gehan/mealplanner/integration/IntegrationService.java
@@ -136,8 +136,9 @@ public class IntegrationService {
             String unit = i.getUnit() == null ? "" : i.getUnit();
             String name = i.getIngredient().getName();
             String text = (quantity + " " + unit).trim();
-            text = (text.isEmpty() ? name : text + " " + name) + (i.getNotes() == null ? "" : ", " + i.getNotes());
-            return new IngredientLine(name, quantity, i.getUnit(), i.getNotes(), text);
+            text = (text.isEmpty() ? name : text + " " + name) + (i.getNotes() == null ? "" : ", " + i.getNotes())
+                    + (i.isOptional() ? " (optional)" : "");
+            return new IngredientLine(name, quantity, i.getUnit(), i.getNotes(), i.isOptional(), text);
         }).toList();
 
         return new RecipeDetail(
